---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lastUpdated = '21 August 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms & Conditions | PACTSOL"
  description="Terms and Conditions governing use of the PACTSOL website and PACTSOL managed B2B sourcing and commercial coordination services."
>
  <section class="legal-page">
    <div class="site-container legal-page__container">

      <header class="legal-page__header">
        <p class="legal-page__eyebrow">
          Legal
        </p>

        <h1>
          Terms & Conditions
        </h1>

        <p class="legal-page__updated">
          Last updated: {lastUpdated}
        </p>

        <p class="legal-page__intro">
          These Terms & Conditions govern your use of the PACTSOL website
          and any sourcing enquiry, supplier interaction, commercial
          coordination, quotation support, or related service offered under
          the PACTSOL brand.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="legal-page__notice">
        <strong>Please read these Terms carefully.</strong>
        By using this website, submitting a sourcing requirement, sharing
        supplier information, requesting commercial assistance, or otherwise
        engaging with PACTSOL, you agree to these Terms to the extent
        applicable to your interaction.
      </div>

      <div class="legal-page__content">

        <section>
          <h2>1. About PACTSOL</h2>

          <p>
            PACTSOL provides managed business-to-business sourcing support
            intended to assist businesses with selected industrial sourcing
            requirements. Depending on the requirement, PACTSOL may review
            information supplied by a customer, communicate with relevant
            manufacturers, distributors, suppliers, or other commercial
            parties, coordinate available quotations or commercial
            information, and present relevant supply options for customer
            consideration.
          </p>

          <p>
            Unless PACTSOL expressly agrees otherwise in a separate written
            transaction document, PACTSOL acts as a sourcing coordinator or
            commercial intermediary and is not automatically the
            manufacturer, seller, distributor, importer, exporter, logistics
            provider, technical consultant, quality inspector, or legal
            representative of any customer or supplier.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>2. Business Use</h2>

          <p>
            PACTSOL is intended primarily for business and commercial
            sourcing activities. A person submitting information on behalf
            of a company, firm, organisation, proprietorship, partnership,
            or other business represents that they have appropriate
            authority to provide that information and to communicate with
            PACTSOL on behalf of that business.
          </p>

          <p>
            PACTSOL may decline or discontinue a request where the intended
            use appears unlawful, prohibited, misleading, inappropriate,
            outside PACTSOL's current sourcing scope, or commercially
            impractical.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>3. Submitting a Sourcing Requirement</h2>

          <p>
            Customers should provide information that is complete, accurate,
            current, and sufficiently detailed for the requirement to be
            understood. Relevant information may include product
            specifications, model or grade, dimensions, standards, preferred
            brand or acceptable equivalent, quantity, unit of measure,
            delivery location, required timeline, intended application, and
            other relevant technical or commercial details.
          </p>

          <p>
            Submission of a requirement does not create an obligation on
            PACTSOL to source the requested product, obtain quotations,
            identify a supplier, secure availability, achieve a particular
            price, or complete a transaction.
          </p>

          <p>
            PACTSOL may request additional information or clarification
            before deciding whether or how to proceed with a sourcing
            enquiry.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>4. Customer Responsibility for Requirements</h2>

          <p>
            The customer is responsible for determining and communicating
            the correct product, specification, quantity, standards,
            approvals, compatibility requirements, performance criteria,
            delivery requirements, and intended use.
          </p>

          <p>
            PACTSOL may assist in communicating or organising this
            information but does not assume responsibility for determining
            whether a particular specification, product, material, standard,
            or supplier is technically suitable for the customer's intended
            application unless such responsibility is expressly accepted by
            PACTSOL in writing.
          </p>

          <p>
            Before placing an order or accepting a commercial offer, the
            customer should independently review all material technical and
            commercial information relevant to its purchasing decision.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>5. Supplier Information and Supplier Participation</h2>

          <p>
            Manufacturers, distributors, suppliers, and other commercial
            parties may provide PACTSOL with information concerning their
            products, capabilities, prices, certifications, availability,
            delivery capability, business credentials, and other commercial
            matters.
          </p>

          <p>
            Suppliers are responsible for ensuring that information they
            provide is accurate, current, lawful, and not misleading.
          </p>

          <p>
            Unless PACTSOL expressly states otherwise in writing, the
            inclusion, consideration, introduction, or communication of a
            supplier does not mean that PACTSOL has certified, approved,
            endorsed, audited, guaranteed, or independently verified that
            supplier or its products.
          </p>

          <p>
            Supplier participation does not guarantee that the supplier will
            receive an enquiry, quotation opportunity, order, appointment,
            preferred-supplier status, or other business.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>6. Quotations and Commercial Information</h2>

          <p>
            Quotations, pricing, availability, minimum order quantities,
            lead times, freight, taxes, payment terms, warranty information,
            product specifications, and other commercial information may be
            supplied directly or indirectly by third-party suppliers.
          </p>

          <p>
            Such information remains subject to supplier confirmation and
            may change before a transaction is formally accepted.
          </p>

          <p>
            Unless expressly stated otherwise in writing, information shared
            through PACTSOL should not be treated as a binding offer,
            guaranteed quotation, reservation of stock, or commitment by a
            supplier or by PACTSOL.
          </p>

          <p>
            Any quotation should be read together with its stated validity
            period, exclusions, taxes, freight conditions, payment terms,
            delivery terms, warranty terms, and other applicable conditions.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>7. Customer Decision and Supplier Selection</h2>

          <p>
            The customer remains responsible for reviewing available options
            and making the final purchasing decision.
          </p>

          <p>
            Unless expressly agreed otherwise in writing, PACTSOL does not
            make the customer's final supplier selection and does not warrant
            that any particular supplier or product will meet the customer's
            technical, commercial, operational, legal, regulatory, or
            financial requirements.
          </p>

          <p>
            Customers should conduct any due diligence they consider
            appropriate before entering into a transaction.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>8. No Guarantee of Sourcing Outcome</h2>

          <p>
            PACTSOL does not guarantee that every sourcing enquiry can be
            fulfilled.
          </p>

          <p>
            Without limitation, PACTSOL does not guarantee:
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>supplier availability;</li>
            <li>product availability or stock;</li>
            <li>acceptance of a requirement by any supplier;</li>
            <li>receipt of any minimum number of quotations;</li>
            <li>a particular price or commercial saving;</li>
            <li>a particular delivery date or lead time;</li>
            <li>successful negotiation between customer and supplier;</li>
            <li>completion of a purchase or supply transaction; or</li>
            <li>ongoing availability of any supplier, product, or commercial term.</li>
          </ul>

          <p>
            Sourcing outcomes depend on market conditions, requirement
            complexity, supplier participation, availability, logistics,
            commercial terms, and other circumstances that may be outside
            PACTSOL's control.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>9. PACTSOL Fees and Commercial Arrangements</h2>

          <p>
            Submitting a sourcing enquiry to PACTSOL is currently free unless
            expressly communicated otherwise.
          </p>

          <p>
            Depending on the sourcing requirement, supplier relationship,
            transaction structure, or services requested, PACTSOL may receive
            a sourcing or service fee from a customer, a commercial
            commission or other agreed consideration from a supplier, or
            another mutually agreed form of compensation.
          </p>

          <p>
            Where a customer is required to pay a fee directly to PACTSOL,
            the applicable fee or fee basis will be communicated before the
            customer becomes committed to that fee.
          </p>

          <p>
            PACTSOL does not publish or guarantee a single fixed fee or
            commission percentage applicable to every transaction.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>10. Taxes, GST, Duties and Other Charges</h2>

          <p>
            Prices or commercial information may be stated as inclusive or
            exclusive of GST, freight, insurance, duties, levies, handling
            charges, or other amounts depending on the relevant quotation or
            transaction.
          </p>

          <p>
            Each party remains responsible for its own tax, accounting,
            invoicing, reporting, registration, and statutory obligations
            unless a specific transaction document expressly provides
            otherwise.
          </p>

          <p>
            Customers should review the tax treatment and total landed or
            delivered cost applicable to a transaction before acceptance.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>11. Orders, Payments and Transaction Documents</h2>

          <p>
            A website enquiry, email, telephone discussion, supplier
            introduction, or quotation coordination does not by itself create
            a completed purchase contract.
          </p>

          <p>
            Where a transaction proceeds, the applicable purchase order,
            quotation acceptance, invoice, order confirmation, supplier
            terms, PACTSOL commercial terms, or other transaction-specific
            document may contain additional or more specific provisions.
          </p>

          <p>
            If there is an inconsistency between these general website Terms
            and an expressly agreed transaction-specific written document,
            the transaction-specific document will govern that particular
            transaction to the extent of the inconsistency.
          </p>

          <p>
            No payment should be treated as required merely because a
            sourcing enquiry has been submitted. Payment obligations arise
            only where applicable commercial terms have been communicated
            and accepted.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>12. Product Quality, Warranty and After-Sales Matters</h2>

          <p>
            Unless PACTSOL is expressly identified in writing as the seller
            of a particular product, product quality, conformity,
            certification, warranty, replacement, service support, and other
            product-specific obligations remain subject to the terms offered
            by the relevant supplier or manufacturer.
          </p>

          <p>
            Customers should review warranty terms, inspection requirements,
            acceptance criteria, return conditions, and other relevant
            product protections before completing a purchase.
          </p>

          <p>
            Nothing in these Terms excludes any obligation that cannot
            lawfully be excluded under applicable law.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>13. Delivery, Logistics and Delay</h2>

          <p>
            Delivery dates and lead times are estimates unless expressly
            guaranteed in an applicable written transaction document by the
            party responsible for delivery.
          </p>

          <p>
            Delays may arise from manufacturing, stock availability,
            transport, customs, weather, labour disruption, regulatory
            requirements, force majeure events, incorrect delivery
            information, or other circumstances.
          </p>

          <p>
            Unless expressly accepted in writing, PACTSOL does not assume the
            obligations of a carrier, freight forwarder, warehouse operator,
            customs broker, or logistics provider merely because delivery
            information is communicated through PACTSOL.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>14. Prohibited or Restricted Requests</h2>

          <p>
            PACTSOL may refuse, suspend, or discontinue assistance involving
            products, transactions, destinations, counterparties, or conduct
            that PACTSOL reasonably considers unlawful, prohibited,
            sanctioned, controlled, unsafe, deceptive, fraudulent, or
            inconsistent with applicable legal or regulatory requirements.
          </p>

          <p>
            Customers and suppliers are responsible for obtaining any
            licence, registration, permission, approval, certification, or
            other authorisation legally required for their respective
            activities.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>15. Compliance and Ethical Conduct</h2>

          <p>
            Users must not use PACTSOL to facilitate fraud, bribery,
            corruption, money laundering, sanctions evasion, unlawful trade,
            intellectual-property infringement, misrepresentation, or other
            unlawful activity.
          </p>

          <p>
            PACTSOL may request additional information reasonably necessary
            to assess a proposed sourcing activity and may discontinue
            involvement where satisfactory information is not provided.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>16. No Agency, Partnership or Fiduciary Relationship</h2>

          <p>
            Unless expressly agreed in a separate written document, nothing
            in these Terms or in PACTSOL's sourcing activities creates a
            partnership, joint venture, employment relationship, franchise,
            fiduciary relationship, or general agency relationship between
            PACTSOL and any customer or supplier.
          </p>

          <p>
            No customer or supplier may represent that it has authority to
            bind PACTSOL unless PACTSOL has expressly granted that authority
            in writing.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>17. Confidential or Sensitive Business Information</h2>

          <p>
            Users should share only information reasonably necessary for the
            relevant sourcing or supplier enquiry.
          </p>

          <p>
            Users should not submit trade secrets, highly sensitive
            technical information, confidential third-party information, or
            information subject to special contractual restrictions unless
            they are authorised to disclose it and have determined that such
            disclosure is appropriate.
          </p>

          <p>
            Where a transaction requires formal confidentiality obligations,
            the parties may enter into a separate non-disclosure or
            confidentiality agreement.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>18. Intellectual Property</h2>

          <p>
            The PACTSOL name, branding, website design, text, graphics, and
            other materials created for PACTSOL are protected to the extent
            provided by applicable intellectual-property law.
          </p>

          <p>
            Users may access the website for legitimate business purposes but
            may not reproduce, commercially exploit, impersonate, misrepresent,
            or misuse PACTSOL branding or proprietary website content without
            appropriate permission.
          </p>

          <p>
            Product names, trademarks, technical materials, catalogues, and
            other third-party content remain the property of their respective
            owners.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>19. Website Availability and Information</h2>

          <p>
            PACTSOL aims to maintain useful and accurate website information,
            but the website may contain errors, omissions, outdated
            information, technical interruptions, or unavailable features.
          </p>

          <p>
            Website content is provided for general business information and
            sourcing coordination purposes and should not be treated as
            engineering, technical, tax, accounting, financial, or legal
            advice.
          </p>

          <p>
            PACTSOL may modify, suspend, replace, or discontinue website
            content or functionality where reasonably necessary.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>20. Third-Party Services and Communications</h2>

          <p>
            PACTSOL may communicate information received from or concerning
            third-party suppliers, manufacturers, logistics providers,
            technology providers, or other businesses.
          </p>

          <p>
            PACTSOL is not responsible for the independent websites,
            systems, policies, representations, security practices, or
            conduct of third parties merely because they are referenced or
            introduced through PACTSOL.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>21. Limitation of Liability</h2>

          <p>
            To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, PACTSOL will
            not be liable for indirect, incidental, special, exemplary,
            punitive, or consequential losses arising from use of the
            website or a sourcing interaction, including loss of profit,
            revenue, production, business opportunity, anticipated saving,
            goodwill, or data, except to the extent that such liability
            cannot lawfully be excluded.
          </p>

          <p>
            PACTSOL is not responsible for losses arising solely from acts,
            omissions, representations, delays, defaults, product failures,
            payment failures, delivery failures, or other conduct of an
            independent customer, supplier, manufacturer, carrier, or other
            third party, except to the extent applicable law imposes
            responsibility on PACTSOL.
          </p>

          <p>
            To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, PACTSOL's
            aggregate liability arising from a specific paid sourcing
            engagement will not exceed the fees actually paid directly to
            PACTSOL for the specific engagement giving rise to the claim,
            except where a different liability arrangement has been expressly
            agreed in writing or where applicable law does not permit such a
            limitation.
          </p>

          <p>
            Nothing in these Terms excludes or limits liability for fraud,
            wilful misconduct, or any other liability that cannot lawfully be
            excluded or limited.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>22. Indemnity</h2>

          <p>
            To the extent permitted by applicable law, a customer or supplier
            will be responsible for losses, claims, liabilities, penalties,
            costs, or reasonable legal expenses incurred by PACTSOL arising
            from that party's unlawful conduct, material breach of these
            Terms, fraudulent or materially misleading information,
            unauthorised disclosure of third-party information, infringement
            of third-party rights, or misuse of PACTSOL services.
          </p>

          <p>
            This provision does not require a party to indemnify PACTSOL for
            liability caused by PACTSOL to the extent such liability cannot
            lawfully be transferred or excluded.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>23. Force Majeure</h2>

          <p>
            PACTSOL will not be responsible for delay or failure to perform
            an obligation where performance is prevented or materially
            affected by circumstances beyond PACTSOL's reasonable control,
            including natural disasters, severe weather, fire, flood,
            epidemic or pandemic events, war, civil disturbance, government
            action, sanctions, transport disruption, telecommunications or
            internet failure, cyber incidents, power failure, labour
            disruption, or supplier failure caused by such circumstances.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>24. Suspension or Refusal of Service</h2>

          <p>
            PACTSOL may refuse, suspend, restrict, or discontinue a sourcing
            enquiry or business interaction where reasonably necessary,
            including where:
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>required information is incomplete or materially inconsistent;</li>
            <li>the request appears unlawful or inappropriate;</li>
            <li>commercially suitable supply options cannot reasonably be identified;</li>
            <li>a party behaves fraudulently, abusively, or deceptively;</li>
            <li>a party fails to meet agreed commercial obligations; or</li>
            <li>continuing the engagement may expose PACTSOL or another party to unreasonable legal, regulatory, financial, operational, or reputational risk.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>25. Electronic Communications</h2>

          <p>
            Users may communicate with PACTSOL through the website, email,
            telephone, or other agreed electronic channels.
          </p>

          <p>
            Electronic communications may be retained as business records
            where permitted by applicable law and PACTSOL's privacy and
            record-management practices.
          </p>

          <p>
            Users are responsible for providing accurate contact details and
            for maintaining appropriate security over their own email,
            telephone, and other communication systems.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>26. Privacy</h2>

          <p>
            Information submitted to PACTSOL may include business contact
            information, sourcing requirements, supplier information, and
            communications reasonably necessary to respond to an enquiry or
            manage a business interaction.
          </p>

          <p>
            PACTSOL's handling of personal information is also subject to its
            Privacy Policy.
          </p>

          <p>
            The Privacy Policy should be read together with these Terms.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>27. Changes to These Terms</h2>

          <p>
            PACTSOL may update these Terms where reasonably necessary to
            reflect changes in services, business practices, technology,
            commercial arrangements, or applicable legal requirements.
          </p>

          <p>
            The current version will be published on this website together
            with its last-updated date.
          </p>

          <p>
            Material changes will apply prospectively except where a
            different treatment is required by law or expressly agreed for a
            particular transaction.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>28. Severability</h2>

          <p>
            If any provision of these Terms is found to be invalid,
            unlawful, or unenforceable, that provision will be interpreted
            or limited to the minimum extent necessary, where legally
            permissible, and the remaining provisions will continue in
            effect.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>29. No Waiver</h2>

          <p>
            A failure or delay by PACTSOL in exercising a right under these
            Terms does not automatically constitute a waiver of that right.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>30. Governing Law and Jurisdiction</h2>

          <p>
            These Terms are governed by the laws of India, subject to any
            mandatory legal rights or rules that cannot lawfully be excluded.
          </p>

          <p>
            Subject to applicable law and any transaction-specific written
            dispute-resolution arrangement, disputes relating to these Terms
            or PACTSOL's services will be subject to the jurisdiction of the
            competent courts having jurisdiction over PACTSOL's principal
            place of business in India.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>31. Contact</h2>

          <p>
            Questions concerning these Terms or a PACTSOL sourcing
            interaction may be directed to:
          </p>

          <address class="legal-page__contact">
            <strong>PACTSOL</strong><br />
            Managed B2B Sourcing<br />
            Email:
            <a href="mailto:hello@pactsol.in">
              hello@pactsol.in
            </a><br />
            Telephone:
            <a href="tel:+917989244563">
              +91 7989 244 563
            </a>
          </address>
        </section>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .legal-page {
      width: 100%;
      padding: 72px 0;
      background: var(--color-warm);
    }

    .legal-page__container {
      max-width: 980px;
    }

    .legal-page__header {
      max-width: 820px;
    }

    .legal-page__eyebrow {
      margin: 0 0 12px;
      color: var(--color-accent);
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.1em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .legal-page__header h1 {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--color-primary);
      font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
      line-height: 1.1;
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    }

    .legal-page__updated {
      margin: 16px 0 0;
      color: var(--color-secondary);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    .legal-page__intro {
      margin: 24px 0 0;
      color: var(--color-text);
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      line-height: 1.8;
    }

    .legal-page__notice {
      margin-top: 36px;
      padding: 22px 24px;
      border-left: 4px solid var(--color-secondary);
      border-radius: 6px;
      background: var(--color-white);
      color: var(--color-text);
      font-size: 0.96rem;
      line-height: 1.75;
    }

    .legal-page__notice strong {
      color: var(--color-primary);
    }

    .legal-page__content {
      margin-top: 46px;
    }

    .legal-page__content section {
      padding: 30px 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--color-light);
    }

    .legal-page__content h2 {
      margin: 0 0 18px;
      color: var(--color-primary);
      font-size: 1.4rem;
      line-height: 1.35;
    }

    .legal-page__content p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--color-text);
      font-size: 0.98rem;
      line-height: 1.8;
    }

    .legal-page__content p + p {
      margin-top: 16px;
    }

    .legal-page__content ul {
      margin: 16px 0 0;
      padding-left: 24px;
      color: var(--color-text);
    }

    .legal-page__content li {
      margin: 8px 0;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .legal-page__contact {
      margin-top: 16px;
      color: var(--color-text);
      font-style: normal;
      line-height: 1.8;
    }

    .legal-page__contact strong {
      color: var(--color-primary);
    }

    .legal-page__contact a {
      color: var(--color-primary);
      font-weight: 600;
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    .legal-page__contact a:hover,
    .legal-page__contact a:focus-visible {
      text-decoration: underline;
    }

    @media (max-width: 1023px) {
      .legal-page {
        padding: 64px 0;
      }
    }

    @media (max-width: 600px) {
      .legal-page {
        padding: 48px 0;
      }

      .legal-page__header h1 {
        font-size: 2.35rem;
      }

      .legal-page__notice {
        margin-top: 28px;
        padding: 20px;
      }

      .legal-page__content {
        margin-top: 36px;
      }

      .legal-page__content section {
        padding: 26px 0;
      }

      .legal-page__content h2 {
        font-size: 1.25rem;
      }

      .legal-page__content p,
      .legal-page__content li {
        font-size: 0.95rem;
      }
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
